./data/57/qa/audit.log:32:**F1 — `must_not [400, 655] "restroom interior"` was a vacuous assertion.** `data/57/walk_truth.json:33` (old). Probe classification shows the cell is **drawn ink**, not room interior: the whole block x 384–422, y 638–672 is solid ink — it is the printed black Restroom sign panel. The assertion "a printed sign is not walkable" would pass unchanged even if the entire restroom/service enclosure were opened up as shopping floor, so it protected nothing. Truth should be a genuine free-but-unreachable cell inside the enclosure (768-cell component, bbox x 260–372, y 640–728). **Fix type: walk_truth point** → replaced with `[345, 665]`, the enclosed service corridor the Restroom arrows point into, behind the sales-floor wall at y=637.
./data/57/qa/audit.log:34:**F2 — five sections of the store had no `must` point.** Kitchen/Dining + Gadgets housewares wing (x 1035–1130, y 328–440) — an entire east department, and the guide misspells the heading `Kithchen/Dining` so no anchor is extracted there either, leaving it completely unguarded; the Seasonal block interior; the Greeting Cards/Gift Wrap/Party/Tech block; Pet + Outdoor Seasonal Selling in the left wing (a 240-pt gap between the aisle-20 and aisle-27 points); Cosmetics/HBA aisles 29–32; and the west Exit/Entrance approach. **Fix type: walk_truth points** → added `[350,292]`, `[350,365]`, `[350,520]`, `[690,400]`, `[748,520]`, `[1075,365]`, `[1112,400]`, `[600,714]`. The Kitchen/Dining and Toys/Fishing points also now pin down exactly the floor that `derive.py`'s auto DELI/BAKERY seal disks would have swallowed had `seal_zones.json` not overridden them.
./data/57/qa/audit.log:36:**F3 — the front enclosed-room warren is several disconnected pockets, only one guarded.** `[700,700]` covered one room; the 603-cell room west of the restroom corridor and the 445-cell room east of the checkstands (walled off from the green café-seating floor by a single drawn wall) had none. **Fix type: walk_truth points** → added `[285,695]` and `[830,700]`.
